::ALG1_U04_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA Standard: Function Notation Bridge Support - no new primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping] If f(x) = 2x + 1, what is f(4)? {
~A. 7 #This uses 2(3) + 1, not the input 4.
=B. 9 #Correct. f(4) = 2(4) + 1 = 9.
~C. 10 #This multiplies 2 and 4 but forgets to add 1 correctly.
~D. 14 #This treats f(4) like multiplication by 4.
}

::ALG1_U04_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA Standard: Function Notation Bridge Support - no new primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping] If g(x) = x^2 - 3, what is g(5)? {
~A. 7 #This appears to use 5 + 2, not the function rule.
~B. 10 #This doubles 5 instead of squaring it and subtracting 3.
~C. 25 #This stops after finding 5^2 and does not subtract 3.
=D. 22 #Correct. g(5) = 5^2 - 3 = 25 - 3 = 22.
}

::ALG1_U04_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA Standard: Function Notation Bridge Support - no new primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping] What does h(6) mean? {
=A. The output of function h when the input is 6 #Correct. Function notation names the output for a given input.
~B. h multiplied by 6 #Function notation is not multiplication.
~C. The input of 6 when the output is h #The notation gives the output, not the input.
~D. The slope of h #Function notation does not identify slope by itself.
}

::ALG1_U04_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA Standard: Function Notation Bridge Support - no new primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping] If C(x) = 7x + 12 gives total cost, what does C(3) represent? {
~A. The cost of 7 items #The input is 3, not 7.
~B. The starting cost only #The starting cost is 12, but C(3) includes the input cost too.
=C. The total cost for 3 items #Correct. C(3) gives the output cost when x = 3.
~D. The number of items that cost 3 dollars #C(3) gives a cost output, not an item count.
}

::ALG1_U04_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA Standard: Function Notation Bridge Support - no new primary MLA standard assigned in approved mapping] From the table x: 1, 2, 3 and f(x): 4, 8, 12, what is f(2)? {
~A. 2 #This is the input, not the output.
=B. 8 #Correct. The output paired with input 2 is 8.
~C. 12 #This is the output for input 3.
~D. 4 #This is the output for input 1.
}
